  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study Tour Dairy Value Chain Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The farming sector in Lebanon faces several major challenges, including economic instability, lack of government support, poor infrastructure, limited market access, environmental degradation and climate change. Additionally, farm management and value chain management are hindered by fragmented farms, reliance on traditional and less productive farming methods, limited access to financing for modern equipment, shortage of skilled labour, and soil degradation. The Netherlands currently supports a local community outreach organization, which has its own school building and Agricultural Industry Incubator, in strengthening its agricultural training program by supporting in the development of a curriculum. The Netherlands has a serious international reputation when it comes to dairy production. This knowledge may be used to strengthen the Lebanese dairy sector. A study tour to the Netherlands will be organised to enhance the understanding of dairy value chain management and farm management of a group of Lebanese trainers. This delegation includes rural community trainers, agricultural extension workers and vocational training teachers who will learn key principles of dairy production, which they can apply and cascade down into their communities for the benefit of local production, productivity and incomes.</narrative>
  </description>
